course: dictionary
lesson: 6965
title: Panama: a country, a canal or a hat
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Panama is a word with three meanings, and the clues tell you which one you need. A capital letter often means a place, like Panama, the country in Central America. The Panama Canal is also a place, a waterway for ships. A small letter, as in «a panama», means a summer hat.
explain: Look at the words around it to decide. «Each ship passing through the Panama Canal uses about 200 million litres of fresh water.» Ships and water tell you this is the canal, not the country or the hat.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «Grandad wore a panama to the cricket.» Could a hat fit there? Yes, so this is the hat. A capital letter and the words around it solve most puzzles.
fact: Panama is a country in Central America that joins North and South America.
fact: The Panama Canal is a famous canal that lets ships sail between the Atlantic and Pacific Oceans.
fact: A panama is a light summer hat, and it is actually made in Ecuador.
fact: A canal lock lifts or lowers boats by filling or emptying a chamber between gates.
fact: Names of places, like Panama and Panama City, start with a capital letter.
exercise: «Panama is a country in Central America that joins North and South America.» Where is Panama? | A large ocean | A ship that sails the seas | *A country that joins North and South America | A type of straw hat
exercise: The Panama Canal lets ships sail between which two oceans? | Indian and Arctic | Atlantic and Arctic | Pacific and Indian | *Atlantic and Pacific
exercise: Grandad says, «I'll wear my panama to the cricket.» What is a panama here? | *A light summer hat | A canal for ships | A type of boat | A country in Central America
test: «A canal lock lifts or lowers boats by filling or emptying a chamber between gates; the Panama Canal's locks lift ships about 26 metres.» How far do the Panama Canal's locks lift ships? | About 2.6 kilometres | Not at all, ships just float | *About 26 metres | About 260 metres
test: «A French attempt to dig a canal in Panama failed after about 22,000 workers died.» Why did so many workers die? | *Mostly from malaria and yellow fever | The water was too salty to drink | Ships sank in the canal | The work was finished too quickly
exam: Which is true about a panama hat? | It is a type of canal lock | *It is actually made in Ecuador | It is made of metal | It is made in Panama City
